[13.301344,"o","Done: 6 of 7 tests pass; the test check fails on one test.\r\n\r\nFailing test: \"absolute zero: 0 K = -273.15°C = -459.67°F\" at calibration.test.mjs:19. It throws `RangeError: Kelvin temperature 0 is below absolute zero`.\r\n\r\nCause: `kelvinToCelsius` at temperature.mjs:21 uses `if (kelvin <= 0)`, so 0 K is rejected. Absolute zero is a valid input, and the test expects it to convert to -273.15°C. The check should be `kelvin < 0`, matching the Celsius guard at line 13. I did not edit the file.\r\n\r\nUnverified: I did not confirm the test's exact expected values beyond the failure output, and I did not check whether any other caller relies on the `<=` behavior.\r\n"]
